{
  "description": "[being built] EZGH Git's branch actions (git.repositories.push, git.pulls.merge, git.pulls.approve) are checked on the repository's name with the branch as the path: ezgh:<region>:org_…:prj_…:gtr_<12>/<branch> (contracts/resources.md). branch is a JavaScript reading of git check-ref-format --branch: it never allows * or :, but does allow /, which org-api's * crosses, so gtr_*/main also matches every branch ending in /main; only a repository's own ID with no * names one branch exactly. The bare repository name doesn't match branch checks, and a deny on it leaves the repository's branches allowed.",
